  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's perception and motion capabilities, separating sensing (uncontrollable) and actuation (controllable). The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are used only when obstacles are detected. Recovery states are conservative and only allow the appropriate turn or scan. The supervisor quickly returns to exploration after recovery, avoids oscillations, and uses full_rotate only as a last resort.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for sensing and motion to reflect the robot's hardware interface.",
    "Specification automaton encodes the exploration policy: prefer random_walk in clear, use move_forward for short progress, rotate on obstacles, and use full_rotate only after repeated blockages. All transitions are deterministic and safe."
